    "readmeMarkdown": "## Telegram (third-party, pending review)\n\nRuns the **third-party** `@iqai/mcp-telegram` server (IQAI) over stdio, pinned to `@0.1.4`. This is built on the Telegram **Bot API** (Telegraf) and is **not** an official Telegram MCP server; it is **pending PuPu review** (`needs_review`). The version is pinned so future releases are not auto-pulled without a re-vet. The bot token is read from the `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` environment variable, injected by the PuPu backend secret store \u2014 it is never written to localStorage.\n\n### Least-privilege bot setup (required)\n\nBefore connecting, create a **dedicated Telegram bot** for the agent and constrain its reach:\n\n- Create the bot via [@BotFather](https://t.me/BotFather) and treat the token as a secret; rotate it if it leaks.\n- Add the bot **only to the specific groups/channels** the agent needs. The bot's group/channel membership **is its blast radius** and is not enforceable in code \u2014 a bot can message, forward from, and pin in every chat it has joined.\n- Enable **mention-only mode** (the package's `SAMPLING_MENTION_ONLY` is on by default) so the bot only reacts when explicitly mentioned in groups, rather than to all traffic.\n- Remove the bot from any chat you no longer want the agent to reach.\n\n### Forwarding is an exfiltration primitive\n\n`FORWARD_MESSAGE` copies content from one chat into another and is gated behind explicit confirmation, alongside `SEND_MESSAGE` and `PIN_MESSAGE`. Only the read-only tools (get channel info, get channel members) run without a prompt."
  },
